# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# The GNSS HAL (overlay/gnss) holds a system-suspend wakelock for the whole of
# a positioning session, so that a guest that suspends itself with its display
# off does not suspend and wake once an epoch for as long as a client listens.
# The platform's rules already let the domain read the receiver node
# (gnss_device); this adds the wakelock.
wakelock_use(hal_gnss_default);
